Lin et al., Nat. Commun. 15, 550 (2024), SM Sec. 3G: eight bands from four
spinful orbitals, and the no-go criterion on two gaps of the one Hamiltonian.
Bands are counted from 0, as pythtb counts them.

1. the model, its two site orbits and all eight bands
   realized group   : #99.164 P4mm1', orbitals at Wyckoff 1a and 2c, 8 bands
   the 1a orbit     : -GM6 + -GM7 + -M6 + -M7 + 2×-X5
   the 2c orbit     : -GM6 + -GM7 + -M6 + -M7 + 2×-X5
   all 8 bands      : 2×-GM6 + 2×-GM7 + 2×-M6 + 2×-M7 + 4×-X5
   atomic limits    : 6 sums of elementary band representations, at
                      1a+1a+1a+1a, 1a+1a+1b+1b, 1a+1a+2c, 1b+1b+1b+1b, 1b+1b+2c, 2c+2c
   the model's own  : 1a+1a+2c, 1 x -E1↑G(2)@1a(4mm1',4mm) + 1 x -E2↑G(2)@1a(4mm1',4mm)
                      + 1 x -E↑G(4)@2c(mm21',mm2)
   srsi_of_model(r) : the invariants of the model and of each site orbit
   P4mm1' #99.164, double-valued: stable real-space invariants, Z x Z x Z x Z2 x Z2   (.structure)
     the whole model: Z-valued (2, 2, 0), mod 2 (0, 1)   (.theta_Z, .theta_Zn)
     each site orbit, its content written m (irrep)_w, and its SRSIs   (.orbits)
       orbitals 0-1 at 1a, 1 (-E1)_a + 1 (-E2)_a: Z-valued (1, 1, 0), mod 2 (0, 0)
       orbitals 2-3 at 2c, 1 (-E)_c: Z-valued (1, 1, 0), mod 2 (0, 1)
   the two orbits have one content and different Z2-valued invariants; the eight
   bands are three elementary band representations at two Wyckoff positions, an
   atomic insulator, not the one whose splittings the supplement tabulates

2. bands 4 and 5: the Z2-valued invariants come from the orbitals, not the bands
   bands 4 and 5    : -GM6 + -M7 + -X5
   atomic limit     : 1 x -E2↑G(2)@1b(4mm1',4mm)
   srsi_of_bands    : Z-valued (0, 0, 1), and no Z_n-valued invariants
   the atomic limit : 1 (-E2)_b, Z-valued (0, 0, 1), mod 2 (1, 0)
   a signed sum     : 1 (-E1)_a + 1 (-E2)_a - 1 (-E1)_b, Z-valued (0, 0, 1), mod 2 (0, 0)
   the Z-valued invariants agree and the Z2-valued ones differ: the Z_n-valued
   invariants are not functions of the content, so a band set has them only through
   a set of orbitals known to carry it, the model's own or an atomic limit

3. splitting(r, bands=6): the six occupied bands against the two above them
   P4mm1' #99.164, double-valued, diagnosed topological: the two sides of the gap cannot both be atomic insulators   (.verdict)
     the bands=6 valence bands, the remaining 2 conduction bands, and all 8 bands   (.n_bands_v, .n_bands_c)
     Z-valued stable real-space invariants: all 8 (2, 2, 0) = valence (1, 1, 1) + conduction (1, 1, -1)   (.theta_Z_total, .theta_Z_v, .theta_Z_c)
     Z_n-valued invariants of all 8: mod 2 (0, 1)   (.theta_Zn_total)
     the valence bands' symmetry-indicator group is trivial   (.indicator)
     possible atomic realizations of the valence bands, and their Z_n-valued SRSIs   (.realizations_v)
       1 (-E2)_b + 1 (-E)_c   mod 2 (1, 1)
       1 (-E1)_b + 2 (-E2)_b   mod 2 (0, 0)
       1 (-E1)_a + 1 (-E2)_a + 1 (-E2)_b   mod 2 (1, 0)
     possible atomic realizations of the conduction bands, and their Z_n-valued SRSIs   (.realizations_c)
       1 (-E1)_b   mod 2 (0, 0)
     no pair of a valence and a conduction realization has Z_n-valued invariants adding up to those of all 8   (.consistent_pairs)
   bands 4 and 5 are among the six: what their atomic limit in section 2 could not
   show, the Z2-valued invariants of the two sides of this gap do

4. splitting(r, bands=4): the same model, the gap two bands lower
   P4mm1' #99.164, double-valued, invisible to the SRSIs: the stable real-space invariants (SRSIs) allow both sides of the gap to be atomic insulators, which does not make them so   (.verdict)
     the bands=4 valence bands, the remaining 4 conduction bands, and all 8 bands   (.n_bands_v, .n_bands_c)
     Z-valued stable real-space invariants: all 8 (2, 2, 0) = valence (1, 1, 0) + conduction (1, 1, 0)   (.theta_Z_total, .theta_Z_v, .theta_Z_c)
     Z_n-valued invariants of all 8: mod 2 (0, 1)   (.theta_Zn_total)
     the valence bands' symmetry-indicator group is trivial   (.indicator)
     possible atomic realizations of the valence bands, and their Z_n-valued SRSIs   (.realizations_v)
       1 (-E)_c   mod 2 (0, 1)
       1 (-E1)_b + 1 (-E2)_b   mod 2 (1, 0)
       1 (-E1)_a + 1 (-E2)_a   mod 2 (0, 0)
     possible atomic realizations of the conduction bands, and their Z_n-valued SRSIs   (.realizations_c)
       1 (-E)_c   mod 2 (0, 1)
       1 (-E1)_b + 1 (-E2)_b   mod 2 (1, 0)
       1 (-E1)_a + 1 (-E2)_a   mod 2 (0, 0)
     pairs of a valence and a conduction realization whose Z_n-valued invariants add up to those of all 8   (.consistent_pairs)
       1 (-E)_c with 1 (-E1)_a + 1 (-E2)_a
       1 (-E1)_a + 1 (-E2)_a with 1 (-E)_c
   the same Hamiltonian and the same eight bands, one gap lower: the criterion
   diagnoses the gap between bands 5 and 6, whose valence side holds bands 4 and 5,
   and not the gap between bands 3 and 4

5. the eight bands along GM-X-M-GM, with the two gaps marked
   bands 3 and 4    : gap 0.661624 over a 41x41 mesh
   bands 5 and 6    : gap 0.581572
   both gaps are open

